{"name":"Saving Light","hex":"#550011","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"saving","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reduction in cost or expenditure.","Something (usually money) that is saved, particularly money that has been set aside for the future."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of save"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saving"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"}],"entries":[{"title":"Saving Light","blocks":[{"text":"\"Saving Light\" is a song by English trance producers Gareth Emery and Standerwick, featuring vocals from Haliene. Roxanne Emery, Haliene, Matthew Steeper, and Karra wrote the song. It premiered in June 2016, during the Electric Daisy Carnival music festival and was digitally released on 30 January 2017. \"Saving Light\" is an uplifting trance song with lyrics about standing up to bullying and supporting victims by being their \"saving light\". Monstercat released the song as part of an initiative called \"Make Trance No. 1 Again\". Their goal was to encourage fans to purchase \"Saving Light\" on Beatport to support Ditch the Label and get the song to the top of the Beatport charts; this was achieved on 16 February 2017."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f2/Saving_Light_Gareth_Emery_Standerwick_Cover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saving_Light","wikidata":"Q29831517"},{"title":"Saving","blocks":[{"text":"Saving is income not spent, or deferred consumption. In economics, a broader definition is any income not used for immediate consumption. Saving also involves reducing expenditures, such as recurring costs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Personal_savings.webp/330px-Personal_savings.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saving","wikidata":"Q319622"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Gareth_Emery_%2836471062352%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Gareth_Emery_%2836471062352%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Gareth_Emery_%2836471062352%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Gareth_Emery_%2836471062352%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Emery (pictured) co-produced the song.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGareth_Emery_(36471062352)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Notaker_miami_2019.jpg/500px-Notaker_miami_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or